\label{def:u-ess}
Given a game $v \in \mathcal{G}^{N, \mathcal{A}}$ and utility function $\mathbf{u}$, a coalition $S \in \mathcal{A}^{\ast}$ is \textit{$\mathbf{u}$-essential}, if either $\mathcal{D}_S^{\mathcal{A}^{\ast}} = \emptyset $ or if $\exists x\in \mathbf{u}\text{-core}(v)$ such that

\begin{equation*}
u_S \circ e(S, x) > \max \limits_{\mathcal{B} \in \mathcal{D}_S^{\mathcal{A}^{\ast}}} \sum_{T \in \mathcal{B}} u_T \circ e(T, x) .
\end{equation*}

Let $\mathcal{E}_v^{\mathbf{u}}$ denote the class of $\mathbf{u}$-essential coalitions of the game $v$.

\begin{equation*}
u_S \circ e(S, x) > \max \limits_{\mathcal{B} \in \mathcal{D}_S^{\mathcal{A}^{\ast}}} \sum_{T \in \mathcal{B}} u_T \circ e(T, x) .
\end{equation*}

Consider the following game, which is a modification of the game examined in Example 3 in \citet{Solymosi2019}: $v(N) = 12, v(\{ 1, 2\} ) = v(\{ 3, 4\} ) = v(\{ 2, 3, 4\} ) = 6, v(\{ 1, 4\} ) = 4, v(\{ 4\} ) = 3, v(\{ 1, 2, 3\} ) = 9$ and for every other coalition $S\in \mathcal{P}(N)$ let $v(S) = 0$.

Let the utility function be the percapita-utility function, that is $u_S(t) = \frac{t}{|S|}$ for all $S\in \mathcal{P}^*(N)$.

The percapita-core coincides with the core, so $\mathbf{u}-$core$(v) = \{ (t, 6-t, 3, 3) \colon 1\leq t \leq 6 \}$.

The percapita-prenucleolus of $v$ is $(3, 3, 3, 3)$. The first iteration in the lexicographic center algorithm (see \eqref{LP1}) gives $t_1 = 0$ and 

\begin{equation*}
W_1 = \{ \{ 3\} ,  \{ 4\} , \{ 1, 2\} ,  \{ 3, 4\} , \{ 1, 2, 3\} ,  \{ 1, 2, 4\} \}.
\end{equation*}

The second iteration (see \eqref{LPk}) gives $t_2 = -1$ and  

\begin{equation*}
W_2 = \{  \{ 1\} ,  \{ 2\} ,  \{ 1, 3\} ,  \{ 1, 4\} ,  \{ 2, 3\} ,  \{ 2, 4\} ,  \{ 1, 3, 4\} ,  \{ 2, 3, 4\} \} .
\end{equation*}

